//     The database stores numeric(28,12)/numeric(38,18); double has 53 bits of
//     mantissa and cannot round-trip those. A string is the only encoding that
//     survives Go/Python/TypeScript/Postgres without a silent rounding step,
//     and it keeps "0.1" equal to "0.1" across languages.
